cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Where does your Core ML model actually run?"
abstract: >-
  Core ML picks whether an operation runs on the Neural Engine, the GPU or the
  CPU, reports success either way, and never tells you what it chose. This
  measures what it chooses and what that costs. On an M4 Pro the Neural Engine
  is the fastest unit and the framework default is the slowest of the three; on
  an M5 Max the GPU is 4.7x faster than the Neural Engine. Same model, same
  batch, same macOS build, opposite answer.
